{
 "paper": "2611.23580",
 "note": "Explanatory slides for the journal club. Figures marked 'schematic' are illustrations, not data from the paper.",
 "slides": [
  {
   "title": "Ultralight dark matter is a wave",
   "text": [
    "For very light bosons the de Broglie wavelength is galactic. Halos are speckled by interference ‘granules’ of size about the coherence length $\\ell_c$, with order-one density fluctuations."
   ],
   "math": [
    "\\lambda_{\\rm dB}=\\frac{2\\pi\\hbar}{m\\,v}\\approx1.2\\,\\text{kpc}\\left(\\frac{10^{-22}\\,\\text{eV}}{m}\\right)\\left(\\frac{100\\,\\text{km/s}}{v}\\right)"
   ],
   "figure": {
    "type": "waves",
    "caption": "Density $|\\psi|^2$ of a superposition of random waves: granules appear and move.",
    "label": "|ψ|² granules"
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "Lensing in the wave-optics regime",
   "text": [
    "Gravitational waves have long wavelengths, so lensing must be treated with diffraction. The amplification factor is a Kirchhoff integral over the lens plane:"
   ],
   "math": [
    "F(w)=\\frac{w}{2\\pi i}\\int d^2x\\;e^{\\,i\\,w\\,T(\\vec x,\\vec y)},\\qquad w\\propto f",
    "r_F(f)\\sim\\sqrt{\\frac{c\\,D_{\\rm eff}}{2\\pi f}}"
   ],
   "bullets": [
    "Wave optics matters when the Fresnel scale is comparable to the granule size: $r_F(f)\\sim\\ell_c$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Granules as a diffraction grating",
   "text": [
    "The projected surface density is non-Gaussian, depending on the halo profile and on $\\ell_c$. Each granule shifts the phase and amplitude of the passing wave, so the lensed signal acquires frequency-dependent modulations."
   ],
   "figure": {
    "type": "waves",
    "mode": "diffraction",
    "caption": "A wavefront crossing the granular field is distorted granule by granule.",
    "label": "GW wavefront through ULDM granules"
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "How big is the effect?",
   "bullets": [
    "About 1% stochastic modulations for moderately magnified images",
    "Above 10% near critical curves or for Type II (saddle-point) images"
   ],
